module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.swap_zero_read_as_a_thrash_refusal

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data swap_zero_read_as_a_thrash_refusal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "swap_zero_read_as_a_thrash_refusal" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "every subject step that runs under the gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired slot contract is judged WHILE IT RUNS by gunbc.host.memory_stall_refusal supervised_subject_verdict from outside the subject, and refused and ended on a refusal -- today the heal round's generations only; the v2-bootstrap subject steps (gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate emitted_subject_build_rows, run through gunbc test) still read memory only at exit through gunbc.host.memory_envelope" } },

  receipts: [
    "**swap zero read as a thrash refusal** (a slot shape that refuses swap -- MemorySwapMax 0 -- is read as if it made a memory overrun END, so a run whose working set exceeds memory.high is expected to fail loudly, and the liveness property 'no thrashing allowed ever' is treated as discharged by static cgroup settings).",

    "INVALID STATE: an authority states, and a consumer relies on, 'swap 0 refuses an overrun' -- gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired's 2026-10-09 ruling note ('swap refused outright, no thrashing allowed ever') and DESIGN's instrument-queue bullet ('MemorySwapMax: 0 refuses an overrun rather than paging it'). cgroup v2 makes neither memory.high nor swap.max an error boundary: above memory.high the cgroup is throttled and reclaimed, never killed for it (Documentation/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.rst); with swap refused only file-backed pages can be dropped, so the run can refault its own text below memory.max indefinitely. swap.max = 0 forbids swap-backed relief; it does not guarantee that excess working-set demand terminates, reaches memory.max, or produces an OOM kill. The exit-time envelope verdict (gunbc.host.memory_envelope memory_envelope_verdict) reads the two terminal endings -- an OOM kill, charged swap -- and a run that never exits produces neither.",

    "OBSERVED (heal, 2026-10-28 to 2026-11-03). The heal job's intermittent 90-minute timeouts are all srv3 runs that needed a second generation (first_generation_equal=false); the rebuilt-seed child went silent after regen.digest for the rest of the step. srv3's slots carry the declared 22/21 GiB with swap 0 (memory.max 23622320128, memory.high 22548578304, swap_max 0 in their receipts). At child begin the orchestrator's slot read memory.current 15636525056: generation 0 had run INSIDE the orchestrator and its corpus was still resident. On srv4, whose slots have drifted to 26/25 GiB with 32 GiB swap, the same rounds completed: child begin 15.63-15.72 GB, slot memory.peak 25.95-26.04 GB, memory.events high 0 (gunbc runs 41638560225, 41632788144, 41632705008, 41630838008).",

    "DERIVED. The two generations' working sets composed in one slot -- about 15.6 GB retained plus about 10.4 GB for the next generation -- which fits under srv4's drifted 25 GiB memory.high and cannot fit under the declared 21 GiB. The drift on srv4 is hidden capacity for this defect: converging srv4 to the declared shape before generation-state lifetime isolation landed would have made the heal round fail fleet-wide.",

    "OBSERVED SINCE FILING (gunbc#15732's own heal run, 41693307466, runner srv3-08, 2026-11-03; slot memory.max 23622320128, memory.high 22548578304, swap.max 0; main's round driver, generation 0 still in the orchestrator). The cgroup-diag lines added by gunbc#15736 read the stall directly. At generation-1 begin the slot held memory.current 15764815872 (anon 12772433920). At the child's regen.digest it held memory.current 22527201280 against memory.high 22548578304, with memory.events high 2196, max 0, oom 0, swap.current 0; anon had reached 20856020992 and file pages had been reclaimed from 2779197440 to 1478139904. Then no line for 43 minutes, until the 90-minute cancel. The slot was pinned at memory.high under throttling, with no OOM kill and no swap: the mechanism this row first filed as a hypothesis. Still unread: PSI (memory.pressure), which neither line printed; the supervised verdict's first refusal prints it.",

    "REPAIR (this row's PR). Three authorities kept distinct: the SLOT says what is admitted (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired); the EXIT verdict reads terminal evidence (gunbc.host.memory_envelope); LIVENESS under the envelope is observed during the run from outside the subject (gunbc.host.memory_stall_refusal supervised_subject_verdict: no progress mark for the declared window AND either the slot's PSI full share at its floor with an envelope event, or the page-thrash verdict over the slot's counters). The heal round's generations are its first consumer, each in its own process group so a refusal ends the whole generation. And the composition itself is removed at its root: generation-state lifetime isolation (v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_admit_generation_begin) -- every generation, the first included, runs as its own process, and the orchestrator's resident set is checked at every transition against its footprint when the first generation began.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable only -- the step timeout contained the harm, after 90 minutes, with no cause attached.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable. Liveness under a host's memory is a runtime fact about external reality; no structure makes a stall unwritable, but a supervisor that executes on every subject step under the slot contract reliably exposes and ends one. Below ceiling while any such step reads memory only at exit.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
